          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.057,
            0.053,
            0.24,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 1,
              "bbox": [
                0.057,
                0.053,
                0.24,
                0.553
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_1.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In convection, heat transfer takes place by the actual movement of particles. Land and sea breezes are examples of the process of convection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.141,
            0.838,
            0.16
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Heat from the Sun reaches the Earth through radiation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.162,
            0.882,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All objects exchange heat with their surroundings through the process of radiation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.202,
            0.883,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Processes of conduction and convection require a medium for heat transfer but no medium is required for the radiation process."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.259,
            0.883,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The principles of heat transfer are utilised in designing houses and clothing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.299,
            0.883,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The continuous movement of water — upward as water vapour and downward through precipitation, passing through soil, rocks and plants, and finally returning to water bodies, is called water cycle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.374,
            0.882,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The process of surface water seeping through soil and rocks is called infiltration."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.414,
            0.883,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Groundwater is the water that seeps through and gets stored in the pore spaces of sediments and the openings in rocks beneath the surface."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.471,
            0.883,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The underground layers of sediments and rocks that store water in pore spaces are called aquifers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.522,
            0.681,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let Us Enhance Our Learning"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
